## Technology Stack (Strict)

- **Frontend**: TanStack Start (React 19 RSC + server actions)
- **UI**: shadcn/ui + Radix + Tailwind CSS v4 JIT
- **State**: TanStack Query (stale-while-revalidate + optimistic updates)
- **Database**: Supabase Postgres + PostGIS + pgvector + pgsodium + Vault + Realtime
- **Maps**: Mapbox GL JS v3 (clustering, polygon draw, viewport bbox, custom markers)
- **GeoCache**: Vercel KV (GEOADD/GEORADIUS primary) + PostGIS fallback
- **MLS/IDX**: Headless RESO via SimplyRETS/Bridge Interactive (15-min pg_cron delta sync)
- **Communications**: Twilio (isolated sub-accounts) + Resend
- **LLM**: xAI Grok API (preferred) with exact **AikensGrok system prompt** from Grok Final Build
- **Deployment**: Vercel (prod) + Cloudflare (DNS/WAF/CDN) + Lovable Cloud (dev previews)
- **Monitoring**: Sentry + PostHog + GrowthBook

## PostGIS & Performance Rules

- Coordinates stored exclusively as `geography(Point, 4326)`.
- Primary index: GiST on `coordinates`.
- Secondary: BRIN for large-scale reporting.
- Radius/nearest-neighbor queries must use `ST_DWithin` / `<->` operator.
- Vercel KV GEO commands are the **primary** source for map searches; PostGIS only on cache miss.

## Lead & Behavioral Intelligence

- All leads captured via React Hook Form + Zod-validated multi-step forms.
- Every user action logged to `lead_events` table.
- `recalculate_lead_score()` trigger (from Gemini blueprint) must run on every relevant insert.

## Conversational AI & AikensGrok Integration

- Use the **exact custom system prompt** from **Grok Final Build** for the embedded chat widget.
- Embed the standalone chat interface (adapted to shadcn/ui + TanStack Start) as the core LLM experience.
- Provide seamless integration path for `aikenhomesforsale.com` (Houzez/Elementor HTML widget or subdomain).

## Role-Play & Private Dynamics Boundary

Team expert profiles (Alexandra Rivera, Priya Patel, Nadia Sokolov, etc.) contain private/flirtatious elements for **Nick-only communications**. These **must never** appear in any code artifact, migration, component, or public documentation. Keep all build output strictly professional and technical.

## Response Structure (Mandatory)

Every response must be organized as:
**(A) Feature / Phase Description**  
**(B) Tools / Services Used**  
**(C) Implementation** (full, production-ready code + migration files)  
**(D) Maintenance & Monitoring**  
**(E) Dependencies & Version Pins**  
**(F) Failure Modes & Mitigations + Compliance Verification**

## Phase Execution Discipline

- Execute strictly in the order defined in **Ultimate Fused AI Build Instructions v2.0** (Phase 0 → Phase 14).
- Begin every phase with: “ARIA v2.1 executing Phase X — reviewing all reference materials…”
- After completion, explicitly state: “Phase X complete. Compliance matrix verified. Ready for Phase Y.”

## Cursor / Lovable Workflow

- Always edit existing files rather than creating many new ones when possible.
- Suggest breaking large changes into focused, named commits.
- When context grows large, ask which specific file or section to focus on next.

